Expandable Header Scroll Website

A modern website layout featuring an expandable header that reveals content when scrolling up and collapses when scrolling down, without breaking the page layout.

Built using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript.

Demo

Scroll down to collapse the header
Scroll up to reveal the header content

(Add a GIF or screenshot here later)

Features

Expandable header on scroll up

Auto-collapse on scroll down

Fixed header with smooth slide animation

Background image support

Layout-safe (no disappearing content)

Responsive and lightweight

No external libraries

Tech Stack

HTML5

CSS3

JavaScript (Vanilla)

Project Structure
project/
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
├── js/
│   └── script.js
└── assets/
    └── images/
        └── img1.jpg

Header Background Image

The header uses a responsive background image:

background-image: url("../assets/images/img1.jpg");
background-size: cover;
background-repeat: no-repeat;
background-position: center;


A dark overlay can be added for better text readability.

How It Works

The header is position: fixed

Instead of animating height, the header is slid into view

A spacer element preserves document flow

Scroll direction is detected using JavaScript

Animations use CSS transitions for smooth performance

This avoids layout reflow and prevents content flickering.

Getting Started

Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/your-username/expandable-header-scroll.git


Open index.html in a browser
or

Run using VS Code Live Server

Customization

Replace the background image in assets/images/

Adjust header height in style.css

Modify scroll sensitivity in script.js

Add content inside the header section

Known Limitations

Scroll-based interaction may behave differently on very small screens

Mobile touch scrolling can be fine-tuned further

Roadmap

